id: pm-swarm-durable-compensation
title: Resume durable native close compensation across dependents
description: Implement durable multi-item native close compensation in a new journal protocol. Current PR intentionally limits automatic rollback to primary-only operations and emits swarm_compensation_partial when native close changed dependents; it never starts a cascade rollback without durable member progress.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: compensation,durability,"gh:unbraind/pm-swarm#32"
created_at: "2026-10-27T18:09:19.394Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T18:43:49.460Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Persist a unique compensation_id and complete immutable member/preimage/history-head domain before any restore; fsync journal checkpoints and parent-directory updates; bind every native restore to that compensation identity and exact target; durably checkpoint restored members; recover without classifying own progress as a peer; preserve peer edits and report typed restored/pending lists; real-process SIGKILL after each restore 0..N with 1-3 dependents converges to exact pre-close item bytes while retaining audit history; peer edit between restores and copied marker tests preserve foreign mutations; packed npm and Bun consumers, docs, focused revert proofs and full CI gates."
parent: pm-swarm-y972
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T18:43:49.460Z",codex-agent,"Current PR deliberately performs zero dependent restores. Native close, auto-unblocking and warnings remain core-owned; only primary-only compensation can resume automatically. This follow-up owns the unique member compensation identity, complete domain and durable per-member checkpoints. The acceptance requires the full after-each-member SIGKILL matrix; the current pre-restore SIGKILL preservation tests are not claimed as that expanded recovery evidence. Pinned SDK remains the version adopted from main."
